  { w: 'admit', p: '/ədˈmɪt/', pos: 'v.', zh: '承认；录取；准许进入', deck: 'senior', ex: 'The art school admitted only twenty students into its program last year.', exZh: '这所艺术学校去年只录取了二十名学生。' },
  { w: 'cheat', p: '/tʃiːt/', pos: 'v.', zh: '作弊；欺骗', deck: 'senior', ex: 'Never cheat in an exam, even when the questions look impossible.', exZh: '即使题目看起来难得不可能，也绝不要在考试中作弊。' },
  { w: 'excuse', p: '/ɪkˈskjuːs/', pos: 'n.', zh: '借口；理由', deck: 'senior', ex: 'Being tired is a poor excuse for handing in nothing.', exZh: '觉得累绝不是什么都不交的理由。' },
  { w: 'error', p: '/ˈerər/', pos: 'n.', zh: '错误；差错', deck: 'senior', ex: 'One small error in the address sent the parcel to the wrong city.', exZh: '地址上的一个小差错让包裹寄到了错误的城市。' },
  { w: 'essay', p: '/ˈeseɪ/', pos: 'n.', zh: '作文；文章', deck: 'senior', ex: 'The essay contest invites students to describe a person who changed them.', exZh: '作文比赛邀请学生描写一个改变了自己的人。' },
  { w: 'lecture', p: '/ˈlektʃər/', pos: 'n. / v.', zh: '讲座；授课', deck: 'senior', ex: 'Professor Li will give a lecture on how robots learn at three this afternoon.', exZh: '李教授今天下午三点将做一场关于机器人如何学习的讲座。' },
  { w: 'punctual', p: '/ˈpʌŋktʃuəl/', pos: 'adj.', zh: '准时的；守时的', deck: 'senior', ex: 'A punctual student never keeps the whole team waiting at the school gate.', exZh: '守时的学生从不会让全队在校门口等他。' },
  { w: 'interrupt', p: '/ˌɪntərˈrʌpt/', pos: 'v.', zh: '打断；插嘴；中断', deck: 'senior', ex: 'Try not to interrupt others even when you disagree with them strongly.', exZh: '即使强烈不同意对方的看法，也尽量不要打断别人。' },
  { w: 'fluent', p: '/ˈfluːənt/', pos: 'adj.', zh: '流利的；流畅的', deck: 'senior', ex: 'Living with a host family for a year made her fluent in everyday English.', exZh: '在寄宿家庭住了一年，她的日常英语变得流利起来。' },
  { w: 'recommend', p: '/ˌrekəˈmend/', pos: 'v.', zh: '推荐；建议', deck: 'senior', ex: 'Our teacher recommends starting each essay with a short outline.', exZh: '老师建议每篇作文都从简短提纲写起。' },

  { w: 'accurate', p: '/ˈækjərət/', pos: 'adj.', zh: '准确的；精确的', deck: 'senior', ex: 'Keep your notes accurate so that you can trust them the night before the exam.', exZh: '笔记要记得准确，考前一晚你才能放心地依靠它们。' },
  { w: 'thorough', p: '/ˈθɜːroʊ/', pos: 'adj.', zh: '彻底的；细致的', deck: 'senior', ex: 'A thorough check of her answers saved her five valuable points.', exZh: '对答案做的一次细致检查为她保住了宝贵的五分。' },
  { w: 'essential', p: '/ɪˈsenʃl/', pos: 'adj.', zh: '必不可少的；极其重要的', deck: 'senior', ex: 'Sleep is essential for a brain that is still growing and organizing memories.', exZh: '睡眠对一个仍在发育、整理记忆的大脑来说必不可少。' },
  { w: 'evidence', p: '/ˈevɪdəns/', pos: 'n.', zh: '证据；迹象', deck: 'senior', ex: 'The team gathered fresh evidence that the lake once stretched much farther.', exZh: '研究团队收集到了新的证据，表明这个湖泊过去的范围要大得多。' },
  { w: 'analysis', p: '/əˈnæləsɪs/', pos: 'n.', zh: '分析；剖析', deck: 'senior', ex: 'His analysis of the poem opened a new door for the whole class.', exZh: '他对这首诗的剖析为全班打开了一扇新的门。' },
  { w: 'curious', p: '/ˈkjʊriəs/', pos: 'adj.', zh: '好奇的；求知欲强的', deck: 'senior', ex: 'The curious boy kept asking why the moon seems to follow us at night.', exZh: '这个充满好奇心的男孩不停地追问，为什么月亮夜里似乎一直跟着我们。' },
  { w: 'patience', p: '/ˈpeɪʃns/', pos: 'n.', zh: '耐心；忍耐', deck: 'senior', ex: 'It takes great patience to teach a puppy to sit still.', exZh: '教一只小狗学会安静坐好，需要极大的耐心。' },
  { w: 'prove', p: '/pruːv/', pos: 'v.', zh: '证明；证实；结果是', deck: 'senior', ex: 'The final match will prove whether months of training were worth it.', exZh: '这场决赛将证明几个月的训练是否值得。' },
  { w: 'eventually', p: '/ɪˈventʃuəli/', pos: 'adv.', zh: '最终；终于', deck: 'senior', ex: 'The lost hiker eventually found the trail after the fog lifted.', exZh: '大雾散去之后，迷路的远足者终于找到了那条小径。' },
  { w: 'gradually', p: '/ˈɡrædʒuəli/', pos: 'adv.', zh: '逐渐地；渐渐地', deck: 'senior', ex: 'If you review a little every day, your fear of exams will gradually fade.', exZh: '如果每天复习一点，你对考试的恐惧就会逐渐消退。' },

  { w: 'breathe', p: '/briːð/', pos: 'v.', zh: '呼吸', deck: 'senior', ex: 'The thin air on the plateau made it hard to breathe at first.', exZh: '高原上稀薄的空气让人一开始很难呼吸。' },
  { w: 'alive', p: '/əˈlaɪv/', pos: 'adj.', zh: '活着的；有活力的', deck: 'senior', ex: 'Folk songs keep the old stories alive in this mountain village.', exZh: '民歌让古老的故事在这座山村依然鲜活。' },
  { w: 'lively', p: '/ˈlaɪvli/', pos: 'adj.', zh: '活泼的；热闹的；生动的', deck: 'senior', ex: 'The secondhand market is lively even before sunrise.', exZh: '这个二手集市在天亮之前就已经热闹起来。' },
  { w: 'raise', p: '/reɪz/', pos: 'v.', zh: '举起；筹集；提高；养育', deck: 'senior', ex: 'The class raised five hundred yuan for the animal shelter near their school.', exZh: '全班同学为学校附近的动物收容所筹集了五百元。' },
  { w: 'rise', p: '/raɪz/', pos: 'v. / n.', zh: '上升；升起；上涨', deck: 'senior', ex: 'Watch the mist rise off the lake as the first light touches the water.', exZh: '看第一缕晨光洒向湖面时，薄雾从水面缓缓升起。' },
  { w: 'lay', p: '/leɪ/', pos: 'v.', zh: '放置；铺放；产（卵）', deck: 'senior', ex: 'Lay the map flat on the desk so that everyone can see the route.', exZh: '把地图平铺在桌上，让每个人都能看清路线。' },
  { w: 'miss', p: '/mɪs/', pos: 'v.', zh: '错过；未赶上；想念', deck: 'senior', ex: 'Hurry up, or we will miss the last bus to the camp.', exZh: '快点，否则我们会错过开往营地的末班车。' },
  { w: 'affect', p: '/əˈfekt/', pos: 'v.', zh: '影响；打动', deck: 'senior', ex: 'Noise from the busy street next door seriously affects my sleep.', exZh: '隔壁繁忙街道的噪音严重影响了我的睡眠。' },
  { w: 'effect', p: '/ɪˈfekt/', pos: 'n.', zh: '效果；影响；作用', deck: 'senior', ex: 'Exercise has a powerful effect on both body and mind.', exZh: '锻炼对身体和头脑都有很强的作用。' },
  { w: 'tear', p: '/tɪr/', pos: 'n. / v.', zh: '眼泪；撕开', deck: 'senior', ex: 'She blinked back her tears and finished the speech with a steady voice.', exZh: '她忍住眼泪，用平稳的声音讲完了演讲。' },
  { w: 'wonder', p: '/ˈwʌndər/', pos: 'v. / n.', zh: '想知道；纳闷；惊奇', deck: 'senior', ex: 'I wonder whether the new timetable will really give us more sleep.', exZh: '我想知道新作息表是否真能让我们多睡一会儿。' },

  { w: 'accompany', p: '/əˈkʌmpəni/', pos: 'v.', zh: '陪伴；伴随', deck: 'senior', ex: 'Her elder brother accompanied her to the interview and waited outside.', exZh: '哥哥陪她去面试，自己在外面等着。' },
  { w: 'attract', p: '/əˈtrækt/', pos: 'v.', zh: '吸引；招引', deck: 'senior', ex: 'The science museum attracts many families with its free night openings.', exZh: '科学博物馆凭借免费夜场吸引了许多家庭。' },
  { w: 'arrange', p: '/əˈreɪndʒ/', pos: 'v.', zh: '安排；筹备；整理', deck: 'senior', ex: 'Please arrange a time that suits both teams for the final match.', exZh: '请安排一个两队都合适的时间来打决赛。' },
  { w: 'blame', p: '/bleɪm/', pos: 'v. / n.', zh: '责备；归咎于；责任', deck: 'senior', ex: 'Neither side should blame the other for the failed talk.', exZh: '会谈失败了，双方都不应责怪对方。' },
  { w: 'burst', p: '/bɜːrst/', pos: 'v.', zh: '爆发；突然发作；爆裂', deck: 'senior', ex: 'Hearing that her poem had won the top prize, she burst into happy tears.', exZh: '听说自己的诗获得了一等奖，她顿时喜极而泣。' },
  { w: 'bury', p: '/ˈberi/', pos: 'v.', zh: '埋；掩埋；埋头于', deck: 'senior', ex: 'The workers buried the new pipes deep under the road before winter came.', exZh: '入冬之前，工人们把新管道深深埋进了路下。' },
  { w: 'charge', p: '/tʃɑːrdʒ/', pos: 'v. / n.', zh: '收费；充电；指控；负责', deck: 'senior', ex: 'The cafe near the library charges nothing for a refill of hot water.', exZh: '图书馆旁那家咖啡馆续热水分文不收。' },
  { w: 'claim', p: '/kleɪm/', pos: 'v. / n.', zh: '声称；主张；索赔', deck: 'senior', ex: 'Some advertisements claim that one pill can cure months of tiredness.', exZh: '有些广告声称，一粒药就能治愈数月的疲惫。' },
  { w: 'glance', p: '/ɡlæns/', pos: 'v. / n.', zh: '瞥一眼；匆匆一看', deck: 'senior', ex: 'Out of the corner of her eye, she stole a glance at the new transfer student.', exZh: '她用眼角的余光偷偷瞥了一眼新来的转学生。' },
  { w: 'hesitate', p: '/ˈhezɪteɪt/', pos: 'v.', zh: '犹豫；迟疑', deck: 'senior', ex: 'If the pain continues for more than a week, do not hesitate to see a doctor.', exZh: '如果疼痛持续超过一周，就不要犹豫，赶紧去看医生。' },
  { w: 'notice', p: '/ˈnoʊtɪs/', pos: 'v. / n.', zh: '注意到；察觉；通知', deck: 'senior', ex: 'Nobody noticed how the queue outside the bakery grew longer by the minute.', exZh: '没有人注意到面包店外的队伍正一分钟一分钟变长。' },
  { w: 'pretend', p: '/prɪˈtend/', pos: 'v.', zh: '假装；佯装', deck: 'senior', ex: 'Some teenagers pretend to be confident while feeling nervous inside.', exZh: '一些青少年表面装出自信，内心却紧张不安。' },

  { w: 'issue', p: '/ˈɪʃuː/', pos: 'n. / v.', zh: '议题；问题；发行', deck: 'senior', ex: 'Water safety has become a heated issue in towns along the river.', exZh: '饮水安全已成为沿河城镇的热点议题。' },
  { w: 'debate', p: '/dɪˈbeɪt/', pos: 'n. / v.', zh: '辩论；争论', deck: 'senior', ex: 'The debate over school uniforms lasted far longer than the teacher planned.', exZh: '关于校服的辩论持续得比老师计划的久得多。' },
  { w: 'major', p: '/ˈmeɪdʒər/', pos: 'adj. / n. / v.', zh: '主要的；专业；主修', deck: 'senior', ex: 'Her major is software engineering, yet she spends every weekend painting.', exZh: '她的专业是软件工程，却把每个周末都花在画画上。' },
  { w: 'majority', p: '/məˈdʒɔːrəti/', pos: 'n.', zh: '大多数；大部分', deck: 'senior', ex: 'The majority of parents support the earlier bedtime policy for boarders.', exZh: '大多数家长都支持让住宿生更早就寝的新规定。' },
  { w: 'various', p: '/ˈveriəs/', pos: 'adj.', zh: '各种各样的；不同种类的', deck: 'senior', ex: 'The club welcomes volunteers with various skills, from cooking to coding.', exZh: '这家社团欢迎拥有各种技能的志愿者，从做饭到编程。' },
  { w: 'negative', p: '/ˈneɡətɪv/', pos: 'adj.', zh: '消极的；负面的；否定的', deck: 'senior', ex: 'Staying up late has a negative effect on both mood and memory.', exZh: '熬夜对情绪和记忆都有负面影响。' },
  { w: 'positive', p: '/ˈpɑːzətɪv/', pos: 'adj.', zh: '积极的；乐观的；肯定的', deck: 'senior', ex: 'A positive mind turns a setback into a lesson instead of a defeat.', exZh: '积极的心态会把挫折变成一课，而不是一场失败。' },
  { w: 'moreover', p: '/mɔːrˈoʊvər/', pos: 'adv.', zh: '此外；而且', deck: 'senior', ex: 'The new reading room saves time; moreover, it lets students test their own ideas.', exZh: '新阅览室节省时间；此外，它还让学生能够验证自己的想法。' },
  { w: 'otherwise', p: '/ˈʌðərwaɪz/', pos: 'adv. / conj.', zh: '否则；要不然；以另外方式', deck: 'senior', ex: 'Start your climb early, otherwise the midday heat will slow you down.', exZh: '要登山就趁早出发，否则正午的暑热会拖慢你的脚步。' },
  { w: 'occur', p: '/əˈkɜːr/', pos: 'v.', zh: '发生；出现；想起', deck: 'senior', ex: 'Most accidents occur when someone is rushing down the stairs.', exZh: '大多数事故都发生在有人匆匆跑下楼梯的时候。' },
  { w: 'remain', p: '/rɪˈmeɪn/', pos: 'v.', zh: '保持；仍然是；剩余', deck: 'senior', ex: 'Despite the storm, the old stone bridge remains safe after a century.', exZh: '尽管历经风雨，这座百年石桥依然安然无恙。' },

  { w: 'annoy', p: '/əˈnɔɪ/', pos: 'v.', zh: '使恼怒；打扰', deck: 'senior', ex: 'Loud phone rings during class really annoy the teachers.', exZh: '上课时响亮的手机铃声真让老师们恼火。' },
  { w: 'embarrass', p: '/ɪmˈbærəs/', pos: 'v.', zh: '使尴尬；使难堪', deck: 'senior', ex: 'He did not mean to embarrass her in front of the exchange visitors.', exZh: '他并不是有意让她在来访客人面前难堪。' },
  { w: 'comfort', p: '/ˈkʌmfərt/', pos: 'v. / n.', zh: '安慰；抚慰；舒适', deck: 'senior', ex: 'Music can comfort a restless mind the night before a big exam.', exZh: '大考前一夜，音乐能安抚一颗静不下来的心。' },
  { w: 'regret', p: '/rɪˈɡret/', pos: 'v. / n.', zh: '后悔；遗憾；惋惜', deck: 'senior', ex: 'Many adults regret the free hours they wasted as students.', exZh: '许多成年人都在后悔当学生时浪费掉的空闲时光。' },
  { w: 'shock', p: '/ʃɑːk/', pos: 'n. / v.', zh: '震惊；令人震惊的事；使震惊', deck: 'senior', ex: 'The final score came as a shock to the whole school.', exZh: '最终的比分让全校都震惊了。' },
  { w: 'whisper', p: '/ˈwɪspər/', pos: 'v. / n.', zh: '低声说；耳语；沙沙声', deck: 'senior', ex: 'The nurse bent down to whisper the visiting hours to the tired father.', exZh: '护士俯下身，轻声把探视时间告诉那位疲惫的父亲。' },
